From: LYOI <lyoi@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: ipq9574: program MISC2 for 10GBASE-R as USXGMII

The 10GBASE-R case only wrote PCS_MODE_XPCS and never touched MISC2, so
the SerDes kept whatever mode the previous configuration had programmed
(SGMII, 0x3).  The digital side then ran XPCS at 10.3125G while the
analog side stayed at 1.25G; link training never completed and the port
reported no carrier.

USXGMII uses the same 10.3125G SerDes rate, so reuse its MISC2 value for
10GBASE-R instead of leaving it at zero.

On JDCloud RE-CS-08 (IPQ5332) this takes PCS1 MISC2 from 0x30 to 0x70,
XPCS KR_STS then reports link=1 and the SFP port comes up at
10000/Full.

--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
@@ -406,7 +406,8 @@
 			goto err_clk;
 	}
 
-	if (interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII)
+	if (interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII ||
+	    interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_10GBASER)
 		misc2 = PCS_MISC2_MODE_USXGMII;
 
 	if (misc2) {
